1. Naming Conventions

A. Unique IDs

Rule: All IDs must be globally unique and follow a structured naming pattern.
Format: [component]-[purpose]-[unique-identifier]
Example: header-nav-contact-btn, user-profile-avatar-img
Optional: Add a project-specific prefix for scoping (e.g., prj-header-nav).

Avoid: Generic names like button-1, image-2.

B. Class Names

Rule: Classes should be reusable but scoped to components.
Format: Use BEM (Block-Element-Modifier) or SMACSS methodology:

BEM Example: .card__header--active, .form__input-error
Project-Scoped Example: .prj-card__header
Dynamic Elements: Append a unique hash for dynamically generated classes (e.g., .user-card-abc123).
2. Customization Structures
A. CSS/SCSS Structure
	•	Rule: Scope styles to components using unique classes/IDs.
	
/* BAD */
.button { ... }
#submit { ... }

/* GOOD */
.prj-contact-form__submit-btn { ... }
#prj-homepage-hero-cta { ... }

B. Dynamic Element Handling
	•	Rule: For dynamically generated elements (e.g., React/Vue components), auto-append a unique ID/class:
	
    // Example: React component with dynamic ID
const Component = () => (
  <div id={`prj-feature-card-${uuidv4()}`}>...</div>
);

3. Automation & Validation
A. Linting Tools
	•	Use Stylelint or ESLint to enforce naming conventions:
	
	// .stylelintrc
{
  "rules": {
    "selector-id-pattern": "^prj-[a-z]+(-[a-z]+)*$",
    "selector-class-pattern": "^prj-[a-z]+(__[a-z]+)?(--[a-z]+)?$"
  }
}

B. Build Process
	•	Add a prefixer plugin (e.g., PostCSS) to auto-add project prefixes:
	
	// postcss.config.js
module.exports = {
  plugins: [
    require('postcss-prefixwrap')('.prj', { /* options */ }),
  ]
};

4. Documentation
	•	Rule: Maintain a STYLE_GUIDE.md with:
	◦	Naming conventions (e.g., "All buttons start with prj-btn-").
	◦	Examples of valid/invalid IDs and classes.
	◦	Links to automation tools and linting rules.

5. Example Implementation
HTML

<!-- Component with unique ID and class -->
<nav id="prj-main-nav" class="prj-nav prj-nav--dark">
  <a href="#" class="prj-nav__link prj-nav__link--active" id="prj-nav-home-btn">Home</a>
</nav>

CSS/SCSS

// Project-scoped BEM
.prj-nav {
  &__link {
    &--active { ... }
  }
}

// Unique ID
#prj-main-nav {
  ...
}

6. Validation Checklist
	1	Uniqueness: Use tools like [W3C Validator](https://validator.w3.org/) to check for duplicate IDs.
	2	Specificity: Avoid overqualifying selectors (e.g., div#prj-header → #prj-header).
	3	Dynamic Content: Test auto-generated IDs/classes in UI frameworks.

By following these rules, you’ll ensure a scalable, conflict-free codebase. Adjust the prefixes (e.g., prj) and conventions to match your project’s needs.